            <ArticleTitle>[Modern treatment of type B dissections].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2858-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rapid classification is essential in the management of aortic dissections, as Type A dissections require surgery, while the optimal treatment of Type B dissections is controversial. Medical treatment with antihypertensive medication and analgesics has so far been the main treatment of uncomplicated Type B dissections, while surgery has been reserved for complications and persistent pain in spite of medical treatment. Endovascular techniques are less invasive than open repair and show promising early results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
